{"title":"Vertical line test","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>vertical line test</b> is a way of determining whether or not a plotted <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Graph_of_a_function\" title=\"Graph of a function\">graph</a> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a>.\n</p><p>The vertical line test states that a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Relation\" title=\"Relation\">relation</a> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Function\" title=\"Function\">function</a> if no vertical <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Line\" title=\"Line\">line</a> intersects the graph in more than one point.\n</p><p>This is because a function cannot have more than one output for any one input.\n</p><p>For example, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/f/8ef862bdd16c2d5356e11735b8c766c402f5e10c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=x^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> is a function because any vertical line intersects it in, at most, one point, while <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1dd4184b561ea747be652fc3dee7fc5e1c5103f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"89\" height=\"18\" /> is not a function (try the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/e/34ea5b6f6de584d56d19a89cc4923a9d9a5cfa41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=0$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />).\n</p><p>In other words, for every x value, there should only be one y value.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Vertical_line_test&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018095157\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.011 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 